From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: the taskbar is not made active when the active window goes away

When the active window is hidden or destroyed, another window becomes
active: its owner, else the next window in Z order that can be. Wine took
windows with WS_EX_NOACTIVATE too, which the system never brings forward
that way -- the taskbar is one, topmost, so right below any closing
dropdown or menu-like popup. When AnyDesk's address dropdown closed, the
taskbar became active and took the keys meant for AnyDesk. Such windows
are now passed over, and the program's own window comes back.

Test: test/noactnext-gate.sh with test/noactnext-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_NOACTIVATE_OTHER).
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -4358,6 +4358,11 @@
     style = get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE );
     if (!(style & WS_VISIBLE)) return FALSE;
     if ((style & (WS_POPUP|WS_CHILD)) == WS_CHILD) return FALSE;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NOACTIVATE_OTHER
+    /* the system never brings a no-activate window (the taskbar) forward
+     * when the window that was active goes away */
+    if (get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_NOACTIVATE) return FALSE;
+#endif
     return !(style & WS_DISABLED);
 }
 
